{"name":"Yeti Footprint","hex":"#c7d7e0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yeti","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unidentified humanoid animal said to live in the Himalayas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yeti"},{"term":"footprint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The impression of the foot in a soft substance such as sand or snow.","Space required by a piece of equipment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/footprint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yeti","blocks":[{"text":"The Yeti, also commonly referred to as the Abominable Snowman in Western popular culture, is a large, hairy, mythical humanoid creature said to inhabit the Himalayan mountain range in Asia. Many dubious articles have been offered in an attempt to prove the existence of the Yeti, including anecdotal visual sightings, disputed video recordings, photographs, and plaster casts of large footprints. Some of these are speculated or known to be hoaxes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Yeti_coloris%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeti","wikidata":"Q129628"},{"title":"Footprint","blocks":[{"text":"Footprints are the impressions or images left behind by a person walking or running. Hoofprints and pawprints are those left by animals with hooves or paws rather than feet, while \"shoeprints\" is the specific term for prints made by shoes. They may either be indentations in the ground or something placed onto the surface that was stuck to the bottom of the foot. A \"trackway\" is a set of footprints in soft earth left by a life-form; animal tracks are the footprints, hoofprints, or pawprints of an animal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Buzz_Aldrin%27s_bootprint_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5877.jpg/330px-Buzz_Aldrin%27s_bootprint_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Footprint","wikidata":"Q2562511"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/1937_yeti_footprints.png/500px-1937_yeti_footprints.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/1937_yeti_footprints.png/500px-1937_yeti_footprints.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1937 Frank S. Smythe photograph of alleged Yeti footprints, printed in Popular Science, 1952","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1937_yeti_footprints.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Yeti_footprint_2%2C_Singaleela_ridge%2C_Darjeeling%2C_1944.jpg/500px-Yeti_footprint_2%2C_Singaleela_ridge%2C_Darjeeling%2C_1944.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Yeti_footprint_2%2C_Singaleela_ridge%2C_Darjeeling%2C_1944.jpg/500px-Yeti_footprint_2%2C_Singaleela_ridge%2C_Darjeeling%2C_1944.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purported Yeti footprint taken by C.R. Cooke in 1944","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYeti_footprint_2%2C_Singaleela_ridge%2C_Darjeeling%2C_1944.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Eric_Shipton_yeti_footprint.png/500px-Eric_Shipton_yeti_footprint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Eric_Shipton_yeti_footprint.png/500px-Eric_Shipton_yeti_footprint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the three photographs by Eric Shipton in 1951 with an ice axe being used for scale.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEric_Shipton_yeti_footprint.png"}